window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["12"]={"https://theconversation.com/labor-slumps-to-new-lows-in-two-victorian-polls-296132":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"517ae165afd5f576da27facfca33e4438ac01e54d1909f7ec20009792427bda8","read":"https://theconversation.com/labor-slumps-to-new-lows-in-two-victorian-polls-296132","bytes":181453,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Labor slumps to new lows in two Victorian polls","by":[{"n":"Adrian Beaumont","r":"Election Analyst (Psephologist) at The Conversation; and Honorary Associate, School of Mathematics and Statistics, The University of Melbourne"}],"pub":"2026-11-10T05:15:26Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["With less than three weeks until the November 28 Victorian election, a DemosAU poll has Labor’s primary vote plunging seven points since September to just 18%, only one point ahead of the Greens. The Resolve poll isn’t as dramatic, but Labor’s 22% is still an equal record low."]},{"k":"p","s":["In both polls, the Coalition would easily win the election with 55–56% of the two-party vote against Labor. In all recent polls, the Coalition has gained to take a big lead. They are likely to win a majority of the 88 lower house seats in their own right. The graph below shows how bad the polls have become for Labor."]},{"k":"p","s":["If the DemosAU poll is accurate, Labor is facing a near-total wipeout, losing left-wing inner city seats to the Greens and other seats to the Coalition and One Nation. Liberal preference recommendations between Labor and the Greens could be important."]},{"k":"p","s":["I believe the recent poll movement is because people are now focusing on the state election, and they want Labor out. Labor has governed in Victoria for the last 12 years and 23 of the last 27."]},{"k":"p","s":["This article also includes a Victorian Pakenham seat poll and two more federal polls."]},{"k":"h","s":["DemosAU Victorian poll"]},{"k":"p","s":["A Victorian ",["DemosAU and PremierNational poll","https://www.heraldsun.com.au/news/victoria/state-election/coalition-surges-to-5644-lead-as-victorian-labor-faces-catastrophic-state-election-wipeout/news-story/cfd77a95d33cd90b152b633f1f4642cb"]," for The Herald Sun, conducted October 30 to November 5 from a sample of 1,562, gave the Coalition 33% of the primary vote (up three since the ",["mid-September DemosAU poll","https://demosau.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/DemosAU-Report-Victoria-Poll-September-2026.pdf"],"), One Nation 21% (up one), Labor 18% (down seven), the Greens 17% (up three) and all Others 11% (steady)."]},{"k":"p","s":["After preferences, the Coalition led Labor by 56–44, a four-point gain for the Coalition. On these primary votes, one of Labor or the Greens would make the final two in most seats, surpassing One Nation on the other left party’s preferences."]},{"k":"p","s":["Labor premier Ben Carroll’s net positive score slumped 16 points -30 (47% negative, 17% positive). Liberal leader Jess Wilson’s was up five points to +13 (38% positive, 25% negative). One Nation state leader Warren Pickering’s was down two points to -20 (43% negative, 23% positive). Greens leader Ellen Sandell was at -20 (38% negative, 18% positive)."]},{"k":"p","s":["In a three-way preferred premier question, Wilson had 36%, Carroll 28% and Pickering 19%. Wilson led Carroll by 48–30 head to head. Some figures are from ",["The Poll Bludger","https://www.pollbludger.net/2026/11/09/demosau-labor-18-coalition-33-one-nation-21-in-victoria/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Victorian Resolve poll"]},{"k":"p","s":["A Victorian ",["Resolve poll","https://www.theage.com.au/politics/victoria/half-of-victorians-open-to-a-one-nation-coalition-as-carroll-faces-labor-wipeout-20261109-p61cjv.html"]," for The Age, conducted November 2–7 from a sample of 1,000, gave the Coalition 30% of the primary vote (up two since the early October Resolve poll), One Nation 23% (steady), Labor 22% (down three), the Greens 13% (down two), independents 6% (up two) and others 7% (up two). This is tied with January 2025 for Labor’s worst primary vote in this poll."]},{"k":"p","s":["No two-party estimate was provided, but analyst ",["Kevin Bonham estimated a Coalition","https://x.com/kevinbonham/status/2119683731883749870"]," lead over Labor by about 55–45, a three-point gain for the Coalition."]},{"k":"p","s":["Carroll’s net likeability was down five points to -16, his worst since he replaced Jacinta Allan as premier in late July. Wilson’s has improved in each poll since July and is now at a record high of +24 (up one since October and up 11 since July). Pickering’s has also improved in every poll since August and is now at +9 (up one since October and up nine since August)."]},{"k":"p","s":["In a three-way preferred premier question, Wilson had 35% (up six), Carroll 21% (down one) and Pickering 15% (up one)."]},{"k":"p","s":["By 48–38, respondents were comfortable with the Coalition governing in partnership with One Nation, but by 50–38 they were not comfortable with Labor governing with the Greens."]},{"k":"h","s":["Victorian Pakenham seat poll"]},{"k":"p","s":["Pickering is One Nation’s candidate for ",["Pakenham","https://www.abc.net.au/news/elections/vic/2026/guide/pake"],", which Labor won by 50.4–49.6 against the Liberals at the 2022 election. A ",["TKW Research/DemosAU","https://www.heraldsun.com.au/news/victoria/state-election/one-nation-poised-to-win-first-victorian-lower-house-seat-amid-pakenham-poll-surge/news-story/0ee84fdba88eed1dda2f35b5f3c60135"]," poll for The Herald Sun, conducted November 4–8 from a small sample of 484, gave Pickering 40% of the primary vote, the Liberals 24% and Labor 14% with no other candidates listed."]},{"k":"p","s":["Despite Pickering’s 16-point lead on primary votes, he’s tied after preferences at 50–50 with the Liberals, indicating a strong flow of Labor and other preferences to the Liberals. Seat polls are unreliable."]},{"k":"h","s":["Candidate nominations for the election"]},{"k":"p","s":["Candidate nominations for the Victorian election closed on Monday. ABC election analyst ",["Antony Green said there are a total","https://antonygreen.com.au/vic2026-candidate-numbers-at-close-of-nominations/"]," of 734 lower house candidates for the 88 seats, an average of 8.3 per seat. That’s down slightly from a record 740 candidates in 2022."]},{"k":"p","s":["Labor, the Coalition, One Nation, the Greens and the Victorian Socialists are contesting all 88 seats and Family First 71, with 91 independents."]},{"k":"p","s":["The upper house has eight regions that each return five members for a total of 40 seats. The scrapping of group ticket voting has resulted in the number of upper house candidates plunging from a record 454 in 2022 to 303, the lowest since 2010. There are an average of 12.4 groups per region, down from a record 22.2 in 2022."]},{"k":"h","s":["Federal Spectre poll"]},{"k":"p","s":["A national ",["Spectre Strategy poll","https://static1.squarespace.com/static/67cd0be72bb18b3c88b9af04/t/6af0f31063b80c7df5dd8a75/1794175760382/Political+Update+November+26-+Spectre+Strategy.pdf"],", conducted October 28 to November 3 from a sample of 2,093, gave One Nation 28% of the primary vote (up two since the ",["mid-July Spectre poll","https://static1.squarespace.com/static/67cd0be72bb18b3c88b9af04/t/6a66a724a5b0f842d4f3f3b2/1785112356745/Political+Update+July+26-+Spectre+Strategy.pdf"],"), Labor 25% (down three), the Coalition 24% (up one), the Greens 13% (up one) and all Others 10% (down one)."]},{"k":"p","s":["By respondent preferences, Labor led One Nation by 52–48, a two-point gain for One Nation. The Coalition led Labor by 53–47, a four-point gain for the Coalition."]},{"k":"p","s":["Anthony Albanese’s net favourability was down 14 points to a record low of -25 (54% unfavourable, 29% favourable). Angus Taylor’s was up five points to -2 (29% unfavourable, 27% favourable). Pauline Hanson’s was down three points to -4 (45% unfavourable, 41% favourable)."]},{"k":"p","s":["In a three-way preferred PM question, Albanese had 34%, Hanson 30% and Taylor 22%."]},{"k":"h","s":["Morgan poll"]},{"k":"p","s":["A national ",["Morgan poll","https://www.roymorgan.com/findings/10377-federal-voting-intention-november-9-2026"],", conducted October 26 to November 8 from a sample of 2,574, gave Labor 25.5% of the primary vote (down 0.5 since the mid-October Morgan poll), One Nation 24.5% (up two), the Coalition 22% (down 1.5), the Greens 15% (down 0.5) and all Others 13% (up 0.5)."]},{"k":"p","s":["By respondent preferences, Labor led One Nation by 54–46, a one-point gain for One Nation. Labor led the Coalition by 51–49, a 1.5-point gain for the Coalition. By 2025 election preference flows, Labor led the Coalition by 52.5–47.5, a 0.5-point gain for the Coalition."]},{"k":"p","s":["Morgan’s polls are taken over a fortnight. Weekly breakdowns had Labor leading the Coalition by 51.5–48.5 in late October, but only by 50.5–49.5 in early November."]},{"k":"h","s":["Essential poll: additional questions on Melbourne Cup"]},{"k":"p","s":["Additional questions on the Melbourne Cup from the ",["late October Essential poll","https://essentialreport.com.au/reports/28-october-2026"]," were released on Cup Day (November 3). On interest level, 68% (up 13) said they had low or no interest, 23% (down three) moderate interest and 9% (down nine) high interest."]},{"k":"p","s":["On betting, 46% (up six and up 11 since 2024) said they’re not interested in the Cup and won’t place a bet, 25% (up one) said they rarely bet on horse races, but would watch the Cup and place a bet, 17% (down one) said they would watch the Cup but not bet and 12% (down six) said they regularly bet on horse races."]}],"chars":6919},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/democratic-republic-of-the-congo":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"8762ac8dee605ed25f0c0604bf34d6db2269fc3d2c3cbad1180995963bf10568","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/democratic-republic-of-the-congo","bytes":104957,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Democratic Republic of the Congo travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-05T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-10-08T13:20:38+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas where FCDO advises against travel"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Areas in Kinshasa Province"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["The districts of N’djili and Kimbanseke in Kinshasa city south of the main access road to N’djili airport, in Nsele commune"]},{"k":"li","s":["The N1 road in Kinshasa Province, between and including Menkao to the west, Kenge to the east, the border of Mai-Ndombe province to the north, and 10km to the south"]},{"k":"hs","s":["DRC-Central African Republic border"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to within 50km of the border with the Central African Republic."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Eastern DRC"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to the provinces of:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Haut-Uélé and Ituri, including the entire DRC-South Sudan border"]},{"k":"li","s":["North Kivu"]},{"k":"li","s":["South Kivu"]},{"k":"li","s":["Maniema"]},{"k":"li","s":["Tanganyika"]},{"k":"li","s":["Haut-Lomami"]},{"k":"hs","s":["South-East DRC"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to Upemba National Park. If you choose to travel to Upemba National Park against FCDO advise, notify the park authorities about your travel plans."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Territory in Mai-Ndombe Province"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to the Kwamouth territory of Mai-Ndombe Province. This is between, and including, the towns of Kwamouth, Bandundu and the southern border of Mai-Ndombe province."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Kisangani airport"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to Bangoka International Airport, Kisangani due to multiple drone attacks in the area of Kisangani airport."]},{"k":"p","s":["See details about ",["why FCDO advises against travel","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/democratic-republic-of-the-congo/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Security situation in DRC"]},{"k":"hs","s":["North and South Kivu"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are in North or South Kivu and judge it safe to do so, and if routes are available, you should leave."]},{"k":"p","s":["M23 rebels and Rwanda Defence Forces (RDF) have captured the cities of Goma and Bukavu and the surrounding areas in North and South Kivu. M23 rebels and RDF captured the city of Uvira in December 2025, and then withdrew from the city in January 2026, though clashes continue in the surrounding areas. The situation remains highly unstable and unpredictable. Routes to depart Uvira, Goma and Bukavu are limited and may change at short notice."]},{"k":"p","s":["The border crossings between Rwanda and the DRC at Gisenyi-Goma and Ruzizi-Bukavu could close at short notice."]},{"k":"p","s":["Goma and Bukavu airports have been attacked and commercial flights are no longer operating from the airports."]},{"k":"p","s":["Support from the UK government is severely limited outside Kinshasa. You should not assume that FCDO will be able to provide assistance to leave the country in the event of serious unrest or crisis."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Tshopo Province"]},{"k":"p","s":["On 23 May, there were multiple drone attacks in the area of Kisangani airport. These incidents have led to disruption to flights. The security situation remains unpredictable, and further disruption is possible."]},{"k":"h","s":["Ebola"]},{"k":"p","s":["On 17 May, the World Health Organization (WHO) declared the Ebola (Bundibugyo virus disease) outbreak in DRC a ",["Public Health Emergency of International Concern","https://www.who.int/news/item/17-05-2026-epidemic-of-ebola-disease-in-the-democratic-republic-of-the-congo-and-uganda-determined-a-public-health-emergency-of-international-concern"],". The outbreak is highly active, evolving and geographically widespread."]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel to DRC read ",["Ebola Disease in DRC","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/news/909/ebola-disease-in-drc-and-uganda"]," and ",["general information on Ebola and similar diseases","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/68/viral-haemorrhagic-fever"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are in DRC read ",["how to reduce your risk from Ebola","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/democratic-republic-of-the-congo/health"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some countries have additional health screening requirements or entry restrictions for travellers arriving from, or who have recently visited the DRC. ",["Check entry requirements","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/"]," for any destination or transit country before travelling."]},{"k":"h","s":["Help and support in DRC"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read FCDO advice on how to deal with a crisis overseas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Getting help in DRC"]},{"k":"p","s":["For help in an emergency from the British government, telephone: +243815566200"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["‘Getting help’","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/democratic-republic-of-the-congo/getting-help"]," for more information on other ways to get help in DRC."]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact FCDO in London"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/democratic-republic-of-the-congo/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC) set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["DRC Embassy in the UK","https://www.ambardc.london/c/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive in DRC."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a visa to visit DRC."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["Apply for a visa through the ",["DRC Embassy in the UK","https://forms.ambardc.london/visa/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Allow at least 2 to 3 weeks for application processing."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some types of visa applications are referred to Kinshasa for a decision. In these cases, if you submit a letter of invitation from the person or organisation you’re visiting, stamped by the Ministry of Foreign Affairs in Kinshasa, you may speed up the process."]},{"k":"p","s":["Consider getting a long-term visa if you are planning to stay in DRC for a considerable period. When you apply for or renew a long-term visa, DRC authorities need a ‘consular certificate’ as part of the application. The British Embassy in DRC can issue a consular certificate for you."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Checks at border control"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have a Rwandan or Ugandan immigration stamp in your passport you may have some difficulties on arrival, but it should not prevent you from entering DRC."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re crossing regularly between Rwanda and DRC you may have immigration difficulties if you have not regularised your residency status."]},{"k":"h","s":["Ebola"]},{"k":"p","s":["You may encounter health screening measures, such as being required to fill in a passenger locator form on arrival and departure and temperature checks, including at airports."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some countries have heightened health screening for travellers from DRC. ",["Check entry requirements","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/"]," for the country you’re travelling to or transiting."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Rwanda","https://x.com/RwandaHealth/status/2057790371657101712?s=20"]," and ",["Uganda","https://x.com/MinofHealthUG/status/2057471796497035293"]," have announced restrictions which impact travellers to DRC."]},{"k":"p","s":["The UK’s Returning Workers Scheme has been activated, due to the outbreak of Ebola disease. Returning health and humanitarian workers should check the latest at ",["UK’s Returning Workers Scheme","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/ebola-returning-workers-scheme"]," before returning to the UK."]},{"k":"h","s":["Departure tax"]},{"k":"p","s":["You need to pay a departure tax of 55 US dollars on international flights and 10 US dollars on domestic flights. You pay these fees when you check in for your departure. Get an official receipt and a copy for each fee. Hand the originals on request to immigration and at boarding and keep the copies."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter DRC, you must have certificates to prove you’ve had:"]},{"k":"li","s":["a yellow fever vaccination"]},{"k":"li","s":["a polio vaccine, in some circumstances"]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s DRC guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/63/democratic-republic-of-the-congo#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You may need a yellow fever certificate for onward travel to some other countries, due to the risk of yellow fever in DRC."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods you can take into or out of DRC. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"p","s":["You may have difficulties when entering DRC if you are travelling with:"]},{"k":"li","s":["satellite phones"]},{"k":"li","s":["GPS receivers"]},{"k":"li","s":["military clothing"]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"p","s":["This guide also has safety advice for ",["regions of the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC)","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/democratic-republic-of-the-congo/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in DRC"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are very likely to try to carry out attacks in DRC."]},{"k":"p","s":["ADF, a militant group with links to Daesh, carry out regular attacks in North Kivu and Ituri provinces, eastern DRC. The majority of its attacks target villages in rural areas, but it has attacked military targets – primarily Ugandan and Congolese armed forces personnel. Attacks have also targeted bars, places of worship, markets and vehicle convoys."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate including in places visited by foreign nationals. Stay aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protests and demonstrations"]},{"k":"p","s":["A range of military and peacekeeping forces are deployed in eastern DRC. Tensions about the presence of these forces and the role of international actors can cause protests in Goma and Kinshasa. There have been large protests against the UN peacekeeping mission known as the United Nations Organization Stabilization Mission (MONUSCO). In February 2024 there were protests outside the British Embassy and other western embassies. Similar protests cannot be ruled out in future. These could be directed at foreign nationals or target UN vehicles and premises."]},{"k":"p","s":["On 28 January 2025, there were large and violent protests outside multiple embassies in Kinshasa, in response to the fighting in eastern DRC. This resulted in an increased security presence and there is an ongoing risk of sporadic protests, which can involve gun fire."]},{"k":"p","s":["Public gatherings and demonstrations can occur with little or no notice and can quickly turn violent."]},{"k":"p","s":["Protests may result in:"]},{"k":"li","s":["the closure of shops and public services"]},{"k":"li","s":["restrictions on movement"]},{"k":"p","s":["In the event of serious unrest:"]},{"k":"li","s":["commercial flights may be suspended"]},{"k":"li","s":["roads may be blocked"]},{"k":"li","s":["international borders may be closed at short notice, particularly those with Rwanda, at Gisenyi/Goma and Cyangugu/Bukavu"]},{"k":"li","s":["internet connections and mobile phone networks may have reduced services or be cut off"]},{"k":"li","s":["military and police presence in Kinshasa and other major cities may increase - this may include stop-and-search checkpoints, especially after dark"]},{"k":"p","s":["To minimise your personal risk:"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow local media for news of any planned protests"]},{"k":"li","s":["leave quickly and do not attempt to watch or photograph any demonstration or disturbance"]},{"k":"li","s":["consider making contingency plans"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep a stock of essential supplies"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep your travel documents up-to-date, including appropriate visas"]},{"k":"li","s":["be prepared to move or go into curfew at short notice if told to by the authorities"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["how to prepare for a crisis overseas","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Stay away from areas where protests are planned, particularly in Kinshasa, Goma and other large cities. This may include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["N’Djili airport, Kinshasa"]},{"k":"li","s":["Churches and other religious buildings and institutions"]},{"k":"li","s":["large sporting stadiums or music venues"]},{"k":"li","s":["universities"]},{"k":"li","s":["political party headquarters"]},{"k":"li","s":["foreign embassies"]},{"k":"li","s":["government and parliament buildings"]},{"k":"li","s":["offices of the Electoral Commission"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not assume FCDO will be able to help you leave the country in the event of serious unrest."]},{"k":"h","s":["Traveling around DRC"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is widespread poverty, social exclusion and health risks in many parts of the DRC. You may be at greater risk of being robbed or attacked in rural areas. Transport and accommodation are extremely limited outside Kinshasa and the major towns, so make travel arrangements in advance. Travel in the company of experienced people or organisations."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be respectful of local customs and land rights, including the necessary permissions for activities. Recent incidents have occurred with local communities when foreign nationals have wild camped without permission."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Street crime and scamming"]},{"k":"p","s":["Foreign nationals are at particular risk of street robbery in Kinshasa, Lubumbashi and other urban centres, especially near hotels and supermarkets in the centre of town. Organised gangs lure people into traps through techniques including the use of children, promising cut-price gold and diamonds, or posing as police or security personnel. Robberies by gangs of street children are common and can be aggressive."]},{"k":"p","s":["In Kinshasa, robberies can be carried out by people posing as taxi drivers or taxi passengers, and are often accompanied by a threat of violence."]},{"k":"p","s":["In North and South Kivu, reports of criminal activity have increased, particularly those targeting the international community. There have been many reports of robberies and banditry in Goma, especially after dark."]},{"k":"p","s":["To reduce your personal risk:"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid walking in the streets alone at any time, especially at night"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not display valuables and cash"]},{"k":"li","s":["use a hotel safe if possible and keep copies of documents, including your passport, separately"]},{"k":"li","s":["use transport organised by a hotel or tour operator"]},{"k":"li","s":["if you must take a taxi, use a privately booked one and do not hail taxis in the street"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Criminal kidnap"]},{"k":"p","s":["Kidnapping is a risk in parts of Kinshasa, including the Limete area."]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been several recent incidents where criminals pretending to be policemen or security personnel have captured foreign nationals and then demanded payment for their release."]},{"k":"p","s":["Criminals may also carry out ‘express kidnaps’, where they capture victims, take them to ATMs to withdraw money, and then release them."]},{"k":"p","s":["Foreign nationals can be perceived as being wealthier than locals and may be at particular risk."]},{"k":"p","s":["To reduce risk:"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid walking in the streets alone at any time, especially at night"]},{"k":"li","s":["Do not display valuables and cash"]},{"k":"li","s":["If you must use a taxi, use a privately booked one"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not hail taxis in the street."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Vehicle crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Carjackings are rare, but lock vehicle doors and keep windows closed when driving. Watch out for armed gangs who may target your car or try to enter it to rob you. Do not drive off the main roads or park in unsupervised areas."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Justice process"]},{"k":"p","s":["The DRC authorities rarely meet their international obligations to notify embassies when foreign nationals have been detained. Even if requested, adequate consular access is not always granted. Keep in close touch with family or friends and ask them to notify the ",["British Embassy in Kinshasa","https://www.gov.uk/world/organisations/british-embassy-kinshasa"]," immediately if you are arrested in DRC."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["Taking photographs of some government and military buildings is illegal, particularly borders or military installations. You risk being arrested and detained. Journalists should not conduct interviews or film without the necessary local permits."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is not illegal in DRC but is frowned upon by many. There is no legal recognition of same-sex couples or same-sex marriage, and there are no specific anti-discrimination laws protecting LBGT+ people. Members of the LGBT+ community are known to be harassed. Individuals may be charged under DRC’s Penal Code for ‘crimes against family life’."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Adopting children from DRC"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against adopting from DRC. The UK does not recognise adoptions made in DRC as DRC is not a signatory to the Hague Convention on Protection of Children and Co-operation in Respect of Intercountry Adoption."]},{"k":"p","s":["The DRC government has not issued exit permits for children adopted by foreign nationals in DRC since 2013 and many are still unable to leave the country. It is illegal for same-sex or trans-sexual couples to adopt Congolese children."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Camouflage clothing"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you wear any military-style clothing you could be misidentified as military personnel and be vulnerable to attack or detention."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Money"]},{"k":"p","s":["Credit cards are only accepted in a limited number of places in Kinshasa and other cities. US dollars are widely used alongside the local currency and a number of ATMs dispense US dollars in Kinshasa. Notes should be in good condition and issued after 2001. Elsewhere in DRC, cash is needed for transactions."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you have access to money, or have arrangements in place for it to be sent to you in an emergency, before leaving the UK."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Democratic Republic of Congo, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],". You’ll need a ",["1968 International Driving Permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," to drive in DRC. You will not be able to buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["Car hire is possible in Kinshasa although self-drive options are limited. Most car hire companies will only let you hire a car with a driver."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Driving standards are well below those in the UK and accidents are very common. Roads in the DRC are poorly maintained, largely unpaved and often not drivable with a standard vehicle, especially during the rainy season from September to May. Inside the cities, including Kinshasa, main roads are often paved but they can be narrow with cars parked on either side. Consider the technical capability of your vehicle and be confident in your ability to operate it. Travel after dark brings increased risk."]},{"k":"p","s":["Public buses and taxis are often not well-maintained, and there is a risk of assault."]},{"k":"p","s":["Security forces operate roadblocks, particularly after dark. If you are asked to produce documents for inspection at a checkpoint, stay inside your vehicle and show them through closed windows."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["UK Air Safety List (ASL)","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/uk-air-safety-list#democratic-republic-of-congo-drc"]," lists all known airlines in DRC that do not meet international safety standards and are banned from operating commercial air services to, from, and within the UK. Check the UK Air Safety List when considering which airlines to fly with. The list is maintained by the Department for Transport, based on advice from the ",["UK Civil Aviation Authority","https://www.caa.co.uk/Commercial-Industry/Airlines/Licensing/Requirements-and-guidance/Third-Country-Operator-Certificates"],". FCDO advises against all travel by air into and out of Goma airport. ",["See why FCDO advises against travel","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/democratic-republic-of-the-congo/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Rail travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["The railways are in a poor state and you should be aware of the increased risk of travel by train. A refurbished route opened between Kinshasa and Matadi in 2015, although services are infrequent and unreliable."]},{"k":"hs","s":["River travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["The ferry service between Kinshasa and Brazzaville stops running in the late afternoon and there is no service on Sundays."]},{"k":"p","s":["Boats and ferries on the rivers and lakes are poorly maintained and often overloaded. As a result of the low safety standards, high river traffic levels, strong currents, shifting sandbanks and poor maintenance there have been many accidents."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding"]},{"k":"p","s":["During the wet season (approximately September to May), heavy rainfall often causes severe flooding in parts of DRC. Check for news of flooding before travelling."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Earthquakes are a risk in DRC, but they are infrequent. The US Federal Emergency Management Agency website has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Volcanic eruptions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Mount Nyiragongo volcano, close to the city of Goma and near the border with Rwanda, erupted in 2002 and 2021, resulting in loss of lives and damage to infrastructure in and around Goma. Further volcanic activity is possible at any time."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of the Democratic Republic of Congo. It only covers regions where the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/democratic-republic-of-the-congo"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/democratic-republic-of-the-congo/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Eastern DRC"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to the provinces of:"]},{"k":"li","s":["North Kivu, including the city of Goma"]},{"k":"li","s":["South Kivu, including the city of Bukavu"]},{"k":"li","s":["Haut-Uélé and Ituri, including the entire DRC-South Sudan border"]},{"k":"li","s":["Maniema"]},{"k":"li","s":["Tanganyika"]},{"k":"li","s":["Haut Lomami"]},{"k":"p","s":["The security situation in eastern DRC remains unstable. Armed groups are active and intercommunal violence can affect the political, security and humanitarian situation. Large numbers of civilians remain displaced as a result of the conflict. Acts of violence, including killing, rape and looting continue against civilians."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are continued reports of towns in eastern DRC being attacked by or falling under temporary control of armed groups. There are continued reports of attacks and kidnappings, including against staff from NGOs and international organisations. Be prepared to leave at short notice via available routes. If you are in an area against FCDO advice, you should be vigilant at all times and keep your security situation under constant review."]},{"k":"p","s":["Foreign nationals travelling in eastern DRC have been left vulnerable, without escorted transport. The risk of kidnap or injury remains high."]},{"k":"p","s":["While British government staff do visit areas of eastern DRC, the British Embassy’s ability to offer support is severely limited."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Peacekeeping forces"]},{"k":"p","s":["A United Nations peacekeeping presence is deployed in eastern DRC. The Congolese army is carrying out operations against foreign and domestic armed groups operating in North and South Kivu and Ituri provinces. Foreign, regional forces are also present in eastern DRC."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Goma and Bukavu"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to Goma in North Kivu and Bukavu in South Kivu in eastern DRC. The situation in eastern DRC is unpredictable, and there is a high risk of ongoing instability, particularly in Goma and Bukavu."]},{"k":"p","s":["The armed group M23 and Rwanda Defence Forces (RDF) have captured and taken control of Goma. Fighting in Goma and the surrounding areas has intensified. Goma airport is currently not operational and is under the control of RDF and M23."]},{"k":"p","s":["On 16 February, RDF and M23 forces captured and took control of Bukavu, the main city in South Kivu. This follows advances south from Goma. On Friday 14 February, M23 and RDF forces captured Kavuma airport, approximately 30km north of the city. Commercial flights are not operating from the airport."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Ruzizi border crossing in Bukavu is under RDF and M23 control and appears open, but the situation remain highly unpredictable and may change at short notice."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is an ongoing risk of protests in the east, particularly in Goma, North Kivu province. These could be directed at foreign nationals."]},{"k":"p","s":["A ‘state of siege’ is in place in the provinces of Ituri and North Kivu. Military administrations with extended security powers have replaced the civilian administrations. On 20 February 2024, the Governor of North Kivu banned vehicles from driving in the province with tinted windows (this includes the city of Goma)."]},{"k":"p","s":["The situation in Goma, Bukavu, and the surrounding areas remains uncertain, unstable and can change quickly. British nationals should be prepared to leave at short notice and have adequate supplies of food, water, medicine etc in case of the need to lock down."]},{"k":"h","s":["Tshopo Province"]},{"k":"p","s":["The security situation in and around Bangoka International Airport, Kisangani, remains unpredictable following recent drone attacks against DRC military assets at the airport. These attacks have been claimed by the M23. Commercial flights are operating as usual, but availability can change at short notice. These border crossings are controlled by RDF and M23."]},{"k":"h","s":["Border crossings with Rwanda"]},{"k":"p","s":["The border crossings between Rwanda and the DRC at Gisenyi/Goma and Cyangugu/Bukavu may close at short notice. These border crossings are controlled by RDF and M23."]},{"k":"p","s":["Following the Ebola outbreak, transit from the Democratic Republic of the Congo through Rwanda is only permitted in exceptional circumstances related to humanitarian missions and essential travel, and is subject to health risk assessment, destination-country, transport operator, and public health requirements, and approval by the Rwandan authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Territory in Mai-Ndombe Province"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to the Kwamouth territory of Mai-Ndombe Province. This is between, and including, the towns of Kwamouth, Bandundu and the southern border of Mai-Ndombe Province."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is ongoing intercommunal violence between ethnic groups over land. The government has deployed a military force to the area. We are not aware of any direct threat against the international community or British nationals. Be aware of the increased violence and potential threat."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas in Kinshasa Province"]},{"k":"p","s":["Due to the risk of violent crime, FCDO advises against all but essential travel in the districts of:"]},{"k":"li","s":["N’djili and Kimbanseke in Kinshasa city, south of the main access road to N’djili airport, in Nsele commune"]},{"k":"li","s":["Kasa Vubu in Kinshasa City, bordered by the N1 Triumphal Road (Stadium), Barumbu District, Lingwala District and the south of the botanical garden"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the N1 road in Kinshasa Province, between and including Menkao to the west, Kenge to the east, the border of Mai-Ndombe province to the north, and 10km to the south. There has been fighting between local militia and Congolese Armed Forces on this section of the N1 road. There are checkpoints on the road and reports of access being blocked. The authorities advise to travel during daylight hours."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is no general emergency medical number in the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC). If you have a medical emergency which requires an ambulance, contact a hospital to make this request."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for DRC","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/63/democratic-republic-of-the-congo#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in DRC","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/63/democratic-republic-of-the-congo"]," including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["ebola"]},{"k":"li","s":["malaria"]},{"k":"li","s":["cholera"]},{"k":"li","s":["yellow fever"]},{"k":"li","s":["mpox"]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of DRC. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ebola"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are frequent outbreaks of serious infectious diseases in DRC. On 17 May, the World Health Organization (WHO) declared the Ebola (Bundibugyo virus disease) outbreak in DRC a ",["Public Health Emergency of International Concern","https://www.who.int/news/item/17-05-2026-epidemic-of-ebola-disease-in-the-democratic-republic-of-the-congo-and-uganda-determined-a-public-health-emergency-of-international-concern"],". The outbreak is active, evolving and geographically widespread."]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel to DRC read ",["Ebola Disease in DRC","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/news/909/ebola-disease-in-drc-and-uganda"]," and ",["general information on Ebola and similar diseases","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/68/viral-haemorrhagic-fever"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some countries have additional health screening requirements or entry restrictions for travellers arriving from, or who have recently visited the DRC. ",["Check entry requirements","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/"]," for any destination or transit country before travelling."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Health Security Agency has ",["Ebola information for humanitarian or healthcare workers","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/ebola-virus-disease-information-for-workers-in-at-risk-countries"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ebola spreads through direct contact with the blood, body fluids or tissues of an infected person, or through contact with contaminated materials. To reduce your risk:"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid contact with anyone who is unwell or showing symptoms of Ebola"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid contact with blood, body fluids and human remains"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid handling bushmeat or contact with bats and other wild animals"]},{"k":"li","s":["wash your hands regularly and follow local public health advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you develop symptoms such as fever, severe headache, muscle pain, diarrhoea, vomiting or unexplained bleeding while in DRC, seek medical advice immediately and avoid contact with others. Symptoms can develop up to 21 days after exposure."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in DRC"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in DRC","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/medical-practitioners"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical care is extremely limited. The Centre Prive d’Urgence (CPU) clinic in Kinshasa is able to cope with basic health problems and to stabilise a patient after most serious accidents. Outside Kinshasa, Western-standard medical facilities are almost non-existent. Medical evacuation to South Africa (or elsewhere) could be necessary. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you take medication regularly, make sure you bring enough for your time in the DRC, and that it is in properly marked packaging."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in DRC"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is no general emergency medical number in Kinshasa or elsewhere in the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some major cities have emergency services, but their level of assistance is limited."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have a medical emergency which requires an ambulance, contact a hospital to make this request. If you are in Kinshasa, you can contact the fire service on 118, and the police on 112."]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Congo%2C%20Democratic%20Republic"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Congo%2C%20Democratic%20Republic"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Congo%2C%20Democratic%20Republic"]]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in DRC","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bereavement-information-pack-democratic-republic-of-congo"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in DRC","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/democratic-republic-of-congo-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/democratic-republic-of-the-congo/british-embassy-kinshasa"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/democratic-republic-of-the-congo/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]}],"chars":30829,"change":"New information and guidance about the ongoing Ebola outbreak in DRC (see 'Warnings and insurance' and 'Health' pages)."}};
